      "content": "\"Finished is a word we use when we're too tired to imagine the next chapter, but that doesn't make it true—it just makes it easier to stop fighting. You've rebuilt before, and even if it collapsed, that effort proves you're not a shell; you're someone who keeps trying, and that's not nothing. It's okay to feel done for now, but 'now' isn't forever, even when it feels like it. You don't have to believe in a future today—just don't let that belief be the final word.",
